  "summary": "Aryabhata, listed by MacTutor with birth in 476 and an uncertain birthplace, wrote the 118-verse Aryabhatiya at Kusumapura (now Patna) and finished it in 499, aged 23. The treatise covers arithmetic, algebra, trigonometry and astronomy, including an explanation of eclipses and the view that the Earth rotates.",
